msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: the IP address every recent member signed in from.
#: includes/Moderation/SafeguardService.php:729
#, php-format
msgid ""
"Your recent members all signed in from the same address (%s). That usually "
"means a proxy, load balancer or CDN sits in front of the site and the real "
"visitor address is not passed on."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Moderation/SafeguardService.php:733
msgid ""
"It is a private network address, which is what a proxy in front of the "
"server looks like."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Moderation/SafeguardService.php:735
msgid ""
"Until it is fixed, BuddyNext treats every visitor as one person: the sign-up "
"limit is shared by the whole site, and a few wrong passwords can lock a "
"member out for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Moderation/SafeguardService.php:736
msgid ""
"Ask your host to pass the real visitor address to WordPress. The usual fixes "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Moderation/SafeguardService.php:737
